Error [jet.InvalidOsDispatchArm]: `.Bsd` is not an OS arm — a `build.target.os` dispatch arm names one OS of the `OS` list, such as `.Linux` or `.Web`
  --> tests/ui/os_target_dispatch_bad_arm.jet:12:9
    |
 12 |         .Bsd -> {
    |         ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Each arm gates code for exactly one OS, so its head is a bare, payload-free OS variant — the same list `#Target(OS.*)` uses — and each OS appears at most once
 Fix: Write one OS per arm, such as `.Linux -> …` or `.Web -> …` (add an `else -> …` for a shared fallback)
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-OSTARGET-DISPATCH-ARM
